  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to the FMoH (Ethiopia) Phase II PBF Pilot in three regions</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In Ethiopia, an PBF showcase project is implemented by Cordaid in the dryland area of Borana Zone since mid-2015. This PBF project was introduced to test how PBF at Health Centre (HC), Hospital, Zonal Health Department (ZHD) and Woreda Health Office (WHO) level can increase quantity, quality and accessibility in hard to reach areas. PBF is a supply side financing mechanism that aims at increasing the output of health facilities and local health authorities by incentivizing pre-determined results. The first phase of the project in Borana ran until mid-2018. Based on the initial success, the project was extended in July 2018. The number of facilities under PBF was scaled up from 9 to 25 (in 8 woredas), and the catchment population increased to 488,556, covering around 60% of the Borana Zone. From 2020 until 2022, the project is continued with financial support from the Embassy of the Kingdom of The Netherlands (EKN). In October 2019, the simultaneous implementation of a second PBF project started with EKN funding, in the coffee growing highlands of the Jimma Zone. In Jimma, PBF is implemented in 13 woredas, covering 4 hospitals, 64 health centers and 1.8 million catchment population.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is about expanding PBF further together with the FMOH as part of institutionalizing PBF in Ethiopia, to three more regions in Ethiopia. This project is supported and approved by the NL Embassy/BUZA in Ethiopia.</narrative>
  </description>
